Same bug as described here https://github.com/mapbox/secret-shield/issues/15
- note the "/bin/sh: Studio: command not found"

I was able to reproduce this bug by copying over the simplified version of `checkInstalled.js` file, particularly [this function](https://github.com/mapbox/secret-shield/blob/main/checkInstalled.js#L12-#L33).
```
const cp = require('child_process');

function checkAndRun() {
  let path = cp.execSync('echo $PATH').toString().trim();
  path = path.replace(/[^:]+\/\.bin[^:]*(:|$)/g, ''); // if it's in a .bin, it's not global.
  try {
    cp.execSync(`PATH=${path} secret-shield --pre-commit -C precommit`);
    return 0;
  } catch (e) {
    return 1;
  }
}

checkAndRun()
```
----> `/bin/sh: Studio: command not found`

When I added the quotes around `"${path}"`, the error no longer occurred. 
```
    cp.execSync(`PATH="${path}" secret-shield --pre-commit -C precommit`);

```

I added a simple unit test here as well.

